module comment_between_pipeline_stages

-- | Plan 69's fourth finding, and the only one of its surface findings that is
-- | a **defect**. This fixture records the defect, so fixing it must fail here
-- | and be reviewed rather than absorbed.
-- |
-- | A comment between two pipeline stages breaks the pipeline: the `|>` after
-- | it is no longer read as a continuation, and `RDX0102` asks for an
-- | expression. Remove the comment and the same five lines parse; a
-- | multi-statement lambda in a pipeline stage is fine on its own, so the
-- | comment is the whole of it.
-- |
-- | `AGENTS.md` says comments are trivia and trivia is never discarded. A
-- | trivium that makes its neighbour fail to parse is the strongest form of
-- | discarding it — which is why this is graded differently from the two
-- | findings beside it, both of which are spellings the language simply does
-- | not have.
-- |
-- | Met twice in the port, at `conformance/redox-fmt/item_text/data_text.sdx`
-- | and `item_text/errors_text.sdx`. Both moved the comment above the binding.
export probe : &Vec<i32> -> Vec<i32>
probe xs = xs
  |> .iter
  -- A comment between two stages.
  |> .map (\n -> n * 2)
  |> .collect
